  "summary_en": "Finnish version of the EU High-Level Expert Group's Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI (April 2019). It sets a voluntary framework: lawful, ethical and robust AI, four ethical principles, seven requirements, technical and non-technical implementation methods, and an assessment list. Embodied AI is mentioned only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Trustworthy AI rests on three components: lawful, ethical, and technically and socially robust.",
   "Four ethical principles: respect for human autonomy, prevention of harm, fairness, explicability.",
   "Seven requirements: human agency and oversight, technical robustness and safety, privacy and data governance, transparency, diversity and non-discrimination, societal and environmental well-being, accountability.",
   "Oversight models HITL, HOTL and HIC are described, with more testing and governance needed where human oversight is weaker.",
   "Chapter III gives a non-exhaustive assessment list, with a pilot phase planned for 2019 and a revision in early 2020."
